  "implementation": {
    "one_state": "Both actual standalone plan types own append::State: original length, one current EOF, one byte ledger and one ordered typed reservation list. Role contexts retain immutable source map/eof facts and membership inventories, not another mutable allocator cursor.",
    "closed_purposes": "DATA, exact physical index and that index map bitmap. Index/bitmap pairs precheck cancellation before committing either reservation. Noncontiguous calls refuse.",
    "byte_semantics": "DATA unique claims and provisional hint clear retain prior collision semantics; index merging retains its prior semantics. All effects in each operation share one original-before/current-after byte vector. Cell/owner authority stays with existing domain qualification and independent audits. The hint-clear fast path additionally checks the original before byte and prepays its lookup; a legitimate provisional set-to-clear still succeeds. This adds paid work and can tighten resource/cancellation boundaries.",
    "maps": "Existing grammar, future-free checks, metadata promotion order, per-domain error boundaries and represented-only rules are unchanged. Complete catalog census remains conditional on existing index promotion; old variable does not gain the future combined gate.",
    "audit": "Index and DATA auditors retain independent expected maps/cursors. Typed builder reservations add consistency checks only. Legacy DATA event-length replay remains staged-event-based; immutable request-derived DATA proof must precede a new combined API.",
    "forwarding": "Ordinary root capacity stays in place while its body is cleared then pointer written on first forwarding. Already-forwarded remainder and retired hidden-body preservation remain unchanged."
  },
